#DESCRIPTION
Classic GEM Challenge magnetic reconnection benchmark (Birn et al. 2001)
with the HYBRID PIC solver (useHybridPIC = T, generalized Ohm's law): kinetic ions and fluid electrons.

Scale and Grid Calculation (Gaussian / CGS Code Units):
  FLEKS uses Gaussian / CGS-normalized code units where:
    curl(B) = 4*pi*J,  J x B = (curl(B) x B) / (4*pi),  P_mag = B0^2 / (8*pi)
  For reference parameters B0 = 1.0, rho0 = 1.0, q = 1.0, m = 1.0:
    Omega_ci = q*B0 / m = 1.0  ->  t_ci = 2*pi / Omega_ci ~ 6.2831853 s
    v_A = B0 / sqrt(4*pi*rho0) = 1/sqrt(4*pi) ~ 0.2820948 code units (28.21 km/s)
    d_i = v_A / Omega_ci = 1/sqrt(4*pi) ~ 0.2820948 code units (28.21 km)
    d_i * v_A = 1 / (4*pi) ~ 0.0795775 code units
    P_mag = B0^2 / (8*pi) = 1/(8*pi) ~ 0.0397887 code units

  GEM Challenge Specifications (Birn et al. 2001):
    Domain: Lx = 25.6 d_i = 25.6 * 0.2820948 ~ 7.2216 code units  (x in [-3.61081, 3.61081])
            Ly = 12.8 d_i = 12.8 * 0.2820948 ~ 3.6108 code units  (y in [-1.80541, 1.80541])
    Sheet half-width: lambda0 = 0.5 d_i = 0.5 * 0.2820948 ~ 0.14105 code units
    Perturbation amplitude: psi0 = 0.1 * B0 * d_i = 0.1 * 0.282095 ~ 0.02821 code units
      (Yields delta_By / B0 = psi0 * 2*pi / Lx ~ 0.02454, matching Birn et al.)
    Densities:
      Uniform background nb = 0.20 code units = 0.20 * 65.15939 ~ 13.03188 amu/cc
      Sheet peak increment n0 = 1.00 code units (total peak n(0) = nb + n0 = 1.20)
      electronDensity0 = 65.15939 amu/cc (n_e0 = 1.0 code units)
    Temperatures:
      Magnetic pressure balance requires n0 * (Ti + Te) = B0^2 / (8*pi) = 0.5 / (4*pi)
      With Ti / Te = 5:
        Ti_code = (5/6) * 0.5 / (4*pi) = 5 / (48*pi) ~ 0.033157 code units
          -> Ti = 0.033157 * 1.21146e6 K ~ 40168.0 K
        Te_code = (1/6) * 0.5 / (4*pi) = 1 / (48*pi) ~ 0.0066315 code units
          -> Te = 0.0066315 * 104.394 eV ~ 0.6923 eV
    Grid: 64 x 32 (dx = dy = 0.40 d_i ~ 0.1128 code units, isotropic square cells)
    Hybrid Configuration:
      useUniformIonPressure = T ensures stationary background ions (uz_i = 0),
      while the electron fluid carries the diamagnetic current via Ohm's law.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.61081                xMin  [code units; Lx = 25.6 d_i = 7.2216 code units]
 3.61081                xMax
-1.80541                yMin  [code units; Ly = 12.8 d_i = 3.6108 code units]
 1.80541                yMax
-0.5                    zMin  [thin invariant direction, 1 cell]
 0.5                    zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
32                      nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
16                      maxBlockSizeX
16                      maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
F                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#FIELDBOXBOUNDARY
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo  (x)
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi
conducting              fieldBoxBoundaryLo  (y; conducting walls matching GEM challenge)
conducting              fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo  (z)
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi

#PARTICLEBOXBOUNDARY
0                       iSpecies
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi
reflect                 particleBoxBoundaryLo  (y; reflecting walls matching GEM challenge)
reflect                 particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#RESISTIVITY
8.0e5                   etaResistivity  [m^2/s; small background resistivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.6923                  electronTemperature  [eV; Te_code = 1/(48*pi) ~ 0.00663 code units, Ti/Te = 5]
1.0                     electronGamma        [isothermal fluid electrons]
65.15939                electronDensity0     [amu/cc; n_e0 = 1.0 code units]

#HYPERRESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaHyperSI      [m^4/s; unused in grid mode]
grid                    etaHyperMode
0.001                   etaHyperCh      [damp grid-scale whistler modes]

#SMOOTHMOMENTS
T                       doSmoothMoments [smooth ion moments to suppress particle shot noise]
1                       nSmoothMoments
0.5                     coefSmoothMoments

#MINIMUMDENSITY
0.0                     rhoMinOhm

#BSUBCYCLE
20                      nBSubcycle

#FIELDINTEGRATOR
rk4                     fieldIntegrator

#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass           Species 0: ions
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
13.03188                rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (nb = 0.20 code units = 0.20 * 65.15939)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
40168.0                 T [K]          ion temperature (Ti_code = 5/(48*pi) ~ 0.03316, Ti/Te = 5)
0.0                     bx [T]
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
gem

#GEMIC
1.0                     b0       [asymptotic magnetic field B0 = 1.0]
0.5                     tp       [tp = 0.5 yields delta_n = 1.0, so n(0) = nb + n0 = 0.2 + 1.0 = 1.2]
0.14105                 lambda0  [current sheet half-width = 0.5 d_i = 0.5 / sqrt(4*pi) code units]
0.02821                 apert    [vector potential perturbation amplitude psi0 = 0.1 * B0 * d_i]
T                       useStandardGem
F                       useUniformPressure
T                       useUniformIonPressure  [stationary ions; electron fluid carries diamagnetic current]
0.2                     nb       [background density ratio nb = 0.2]
standard                pertType

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.005                   dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI  [m; lNorm = 100 km]
1.0e5                   uNormSI  [m/s; uNorm = 100 km/s]

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
4                       nParticle per cell in X
4                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
0.5                     dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
1.0                     TimeMax

#RUN
